ompensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 221 people. Revenue per employee of $73K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $80K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 14\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["uniQure N.V. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.7B market cap on $16M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -47% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -110% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $178M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 110% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 1151% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the 